  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the SwiftHFR maintainers, we want a real capture of the `img3.super-h.fr` medium rendition, so that the `.md.` → full-size rule of #917 (sourced today from legacy code only) can be labelled **verified** in `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md` §LOT-056.\n\n### To capture (Mac, anonymized per `docs/FIXTURES.md`; do not hand-build)\n\n1. The upload answer of a **large** image (the existing `U01`/`U02` are 16×16, where `image.medium` is `null`), showing `image.medium.url`. Redact `delete_url`/`delete_hash` and the key.\n2. One cookie-less GET of the `.md.` URL and one of its full-size URL (`<name>.<ext>`): status, content type, size, and `Referer` behaviour.\n3. Optional: one GET of the `.th.` URL of the same image, for comparison.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Captures added under the fixtures corpus, anonymized and checked.\n- [ ] HFR-PROTOCOL §LOT-056 \"Medium rendition\" line moves from **code** to **verified** (or records the difference).\n\nRefs #917.",
